Ladybird centers the border box of an mtable on its own math axis. Blink
supplies MathTableBaseline() from TableLayoutAlgorithm, WebKit uses
RenderMathMLTable::firstLineBaseline(), and Gecko handles axis alignment
in nsMathMLmtableWrapperFrame::Reflow().

Chrome 158.0.8127.37, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 all centered a
280px stretchy fence on a 240px eight-row matrix in the test font. All
three also used the axis of the table font with asymmetric borders,
padding, or margins, and with an explicit table height.
